            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all four changed paths. The new reviewverdict package is a pure parser: it reads no file, runs no command, and has no network or privilege surface.",
              "Parse refuses a reply unless it is valid UTF-8, has no duplicate keys, has no unknown members (matched by exact name), has every member non-null, answers each finding id exactly once, uses enum values the contract lists, and carries evidence. Each refusal returns no verdicts, so a refused reply cannot clear a finding. This is fail-closed.",
              "The ErrUnanswered rule and the NotRun-is-not-NotReproduced distinction stop an unchecked finding from being read as one that did not reproduce. No path in the candidate silently accepts a missing or unverified verdict.",
              "Untrusted verifier output is handled with strict decoding through jsonstrict, and exact-name checks cover the case-insensitive matching of encoding/json. Error messages quote ids with %q, so there is no injection into logs. No secrets, dependencies, or lockfiles changed.",
              "engine/architecture_test.go only registers the new package in the Domain ring and adds a comment, so no layering guard is weakened."
            ]
          }
        }
